			<div class="entry">
				<p>For those of you who use NHibernate you may find this convenient, if you don&#8217;t already have your own.&nbsp; Below is a C# code snippet for creating a public virtual property (code and file are both there).&nbsp; Just put it in your <em>&lt;Visual Studio 2005/2008&gt;\Code Snippets\Visual C#\My Code Snippets</em> folder and you&#8217;re off and running.&nbsp; No restart required.</p>
<p><strong><a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/cfs-file.ashx/__key/CommunityServer.Components.PostAttachments/00.00.00.06.84/propv.snippet">File</a></strong></p>
